<title>GERMANY: Parliament committee details German 1997 budget.</title>
<headline>Parliament committee details German 1997 budget.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany's parliamentary budget committee on Friday approved the following 1997 federal budget. Second and third readings in parliament on the measure are expected in two weeks. (All figures in millions of marks).</p>
<p>				Original govt draft  Committee version</p>
<p>    President's office		     32.7		   31.8</p>
<p>    Lower house of parliament	   913.4		  905.7</p>
<p>    Upper house of parliament	    27.2		   26.4</p>
<p>    Chancellery			     582.0		  547.8</p>
<p>    Foreign				 3,634.0		3,551.3</p>
<p>    Interior				8,809.8		8,629.2</p>
<p>    Justice				   701.8		  706.2</p>
<p>    Finance				 8,302.2		7,905.8</p>
<p>    Economics			    17,026.0	     16,607.4</p>
<p>    Food, Agric. and Forestry	12,060.0	     11,795.3</p>
<p>    Labour				122,118.4	    127,793.6</p>
<p>    Transport			    45,050.0	     44,572.8</p>
<p>    Post and Telecommunications	 358.2		  344.0</p>
<p>    Defence				46,500.0	     46,290.3</p>
<p>    Health				    751.9		  725.6</p>
<p>    Environment			   1,319.5		1,285.1</p>
<p>    Family				 11,725.9	     11,696.7</p>
<p>    Constitutional Court		   29.8		   29.5</p>
<p>    Audit Office			     77.2		   77.2</p>
<p>    Economic Cooperation and Devt   7,803.1		7,651.0</p>
<p>    Planning			     10,450.2	     10,490.8</p>
<p>    Education and Research	   15,000.0	     14,818.5</p>
<p>    Debt service			 89,221.9	     86,022.8</p>
<p>    Civil service pensions	   15,927.9	     15,859.9</p>
<p>    General Financial Admin	  21,777.1	     21,535.5</p>
<p>    TOTAL				 440,200.0	    439,900.0</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures do not add up exactly due to rounding.</p>
<p>-- Douglas Busvine, Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
</text>
